From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 17:26:15 -0400
Subject: Limit max image allocation size to 1GB.

This limit matches the Vulkan backend and Mesa's MAX_TEXTURE_MBYTES.

Covered entry points:
glTexImage2D
glCompressedTexImage2D
glTexStorage2DEXT
glTexStorage2D
glTexImage3D
glTexStorage3D
glTexStorage3DEXT
glRenderbufferStorage
glRenderbufferStorageMultisample
glRenderbufferStorageMultisampleEXT
glTexStorage2DMultisample
glTexStorage2DMultisampleANGLE
glTexStorage3DMultisample

Fixed: angleproject:485900022
Change-Id: I60978b6296ca0512d4720279868f8965a0a3292d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/7738926
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
Prerequisite for the following PowerVR 3D texture fix: introduces
Limitations::maxTextureBytes and ValidImageAllocationSize(), which that
fix modifies. Cherry-picked from ANGLE main 6bbde839bd (Change-Id
I60978b6296ca0512d4720279868f8965a0a3292d). Conflicts were limited to
tests (ReadPixelsTest.cpp, TextureTest.cpp; both sides kept) and the
autogen feature-name lists. Note that this adds a 1 GB per-texture
allocation limit on the GL/D3D backends that M148 ANGLE did not have.

